+# Spill tier for kept prompt states (SPILL_GIB, off by default). Kept prompt states that leave the KV pool are written
+# to local disk on every Spark; a later request that extends one reads it back instead of prefilling again, across a
+# clean restart too. SPILL_GIB=0 (the default) passes no flag, mounts no directory and skips the engine paths. Writes
+# go to SPILL_DIR (mounted /spill) as one 0600 file per prompt per rank under spill-<hash>/rank<N>/, each 8 MiB block
+# CRC-32'd and checked on read; rank 0 decides every save, eviction, load and flush and the others follow its ops, so
+# every rank holds the same index. Settings in scripts/config.sh: SPILL_GIB, SPILL_DIR, SPILL_HIGHWATER (0.70),
+# SPILL_MIN_TOKENS (8192), SPILL_MIN_FREE_GIB (50), SPILL_FLUSH_S (60); a clean stop flushes within SPILL_FLUSH_S and
+# STOP_TIMEOUT is raised to cover it. Counters: /health's "spill", /metrics' tensorfold_health:spill_*.
+#
+# Applies after 0063 (which decides what leaves first), 0071-0075, 0077 and 0078. Three fits to this recipe:
+#   * 0072's display span: the spanned latent planes sit over two host registrations and CUDA refuses a memcpy across
+#     them, so the store takes their names (spanned=) and moves those rows through an 8 MiB device buffer with the same
+#     bitwise_or kernel 0072 uses -- in both directions (spill.py's _by_kernel). Other planes copy as before.
+#   * 0073's queued cancellation: _cancel_waiting also reaps requests whose stored prompt has been read (ready) and
+#     those still reading (loading), and _cancel_item drops the request's id from staged. The flush wake-up item is
+#     GlmScheduler._Flush (emit = None), so 0073's queue scans pass it by.
+#   * 0074's compaction moves rows through pool.move, which this patch's guard wraps, so a move waits for a pending
+#     copy of those rows; a take-over in place waits in _rewrites.
+#
+# 0078 (take-over decided first, copied after) and this patch both rewrite the tail of the single-stream _take_over.
+# Merged, not stacked: 0078's two-pass shape stands (sizes decide, drops run, only survivors are cloned, and
+# empty_cache fires on over_budget -- the NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY fix), and this patch's two spill steps move onto it. The
+# per-snapshot write of a state whose DFlash2 window save_rows dropped now sits in the second loop, beside the
+# save_rows it reads from; _spill_wait runs after both loops, so every pending copy leaves the device before
+# empty_cache returns the rows to torch's pool and before the next prefill overwrites the live caches.
+#
+# Upstream: MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#78 by @wojo (its patch 0078, renumbered 0084 here;
+# 0078 is taken). The same tier for upstream TensorFold's one-stream engine is ashhart/TensorFold#427 (drop the
+# engine.py half of this patch once that merges). Closes #57.
+
